  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Save lives, reduce suffering and contribute towards prevention of negative copin</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of this project is to provide access to food, water, sanitation, and hygiene, as well as adequate protection services. Underserved 10  Internally Displaced Person (IDP) locations in  Al -Faw , Al Mathna ,Kuliat Al -Mujtama, Al -muthaf, Al -Zera&apos;a office, Hawsh Al -Zera&apos;a, Adhban Factory, Bateh Al -Khlait, Al -Masheer and Al -Qoaz Marib and Alwadi district of Marib Governorate, Yemen , who face the threat of famine, disease, and direct protection.  A total of 21,371  IDPs will be assisted (6,283 men, 6,176 women, 4,531 boys, 4,381 girls). Improved access to basic needs for the most vulnerable and food insecure 700 IDP households (HHs) through life saving cash assistance, 21,371 crises -affected individuals including men, women, boys and girls have improved equitable access to safe water, adequate sanitation and hygiene awareness through engaging them in project activities&apos;.  Protection risks of 800 households/individuals are reduced through direct protection assistance in the community centre as well as Community initiatives.</narrative>
  </description>
